\subsubsection{Claim 2: Stochasticity alone provides limited improvements}

% Table~\ref{tab:coverage_gap}, ~\ref{tab:discontinuous}, and ~\ref{tab:angle_disparity} show that stochastic methods, such as 3DGS-MCMC~\cite{mcmc} and MH-3DGS~\cite{mh3dgs}, generally outperform photometric optimization and geometric regularization baselines, suggesting that stochastic exploration helps Gaussian updates escape locally biased optimization. 
Table~\ref{tab:coverage_gap}, ~\ref{tab:discontinuous}, and ~\ref{tab:angle_disparity} show that stochastic exploration can improve over purely photometric optimization and geometric regularization baselines. In particular, 3DGS-MCMC~\cite{mcmc} is consistently competitive across all biased viewpoint settings, suggesting that stochastic updates help Gaussian primitives escape locally biased optimization.

% However, these results also suggest that the stochasticity alone is still limited, as the performance of MCMC-based methods is generally inferior to our GS-LSS, and the performance gap increases monotonically with the severity of the bias.
However, these results also suggest that hand-crafted stochasticity alone is still limited, as the performance of MCMC-based methods is generally inferior to our GS-LSS, and the performance gap widens as the bias becomes more severe.
% Taking the systematic coverage gap setting as an example, the PSNR gap between 3DGS-MCMC~\cite{mcmc} and GS-LSS hovers around 0.4 dB and 0.2 dB on Mip-NeRF 360~\cite{mipnerf360} and Tanks \& Temples~\cite{tankstemples} respectively when the gap size is lower than 40$^\circ$, but increases all the way to 1.35 dB and 0.37 dB at 100$^\circ$. 
Taking the systematic coverage gap as an example, on Mip-NeRF 360~\cite{mipnerf360} the PSNR advantage of GS-LSS over 3DGS-MCMC~\cite{mcmc} grows monotonically with the gap size, widening from 0.52 dB at the mildest 20$^\circ$ gap to 1.60 dB at 100$^\circ$. A consistent advantage is also observed on Tanks \& Temples~\cite{tankstemples}, where GS-LSS outperforms 3DGS-MCMC at every gap size by 0.10-0.43 dB PSNR.
