\subsubsection{Claim 2: Stochasticity alone provides limited improvements}

Tables~\ref{tab:coverage_gap}--\ref{tab:angle_disparity} show that stochastic baselines are competitive, but hand-crafted stochasticity often remains below GS-LSS. In the systematic coverage-gap setting, the PSNR advantage over 3DGS-MCMC~\cite{mcmc} grows from 0.52 to 1.60 dB on Mip-NeRF 360~\cite{mipnerf360}, and remains 0.10--0.43 dB on Tanks \& Temples~\cite{tankstemples}. This suggests that stochasticity helps escape biased local minima but remains limited when guided mainly by photometric gradients.

