\subsubsection{Claim 3: CPF-guided observed-support regularization improves biased-view robustness}

Across the three biased-viewpoint settings, GS-LSS is best or highly competitive against deterministic, geometric, and stochastic baselines. The results support the design choice of using CPF-guided observed-support regularization to complement photometric optimization and hand-crafted stochasticity. Qualitative comparisons in Fig.~\ref{visual_comparison} show more coherent geometry and fewer visible artifacts in the displayed cases, consistent with the floater-density visualization in Fig.~\ref{perspective_overfitting}.

